<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Holy Spirit Movement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1986">1986</a>–<a href="/years/1987">1987</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Holy Spirit Movement was a rebel movement in northern Uganda led by Alice Auma, known as Alice Lakwena, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acholi">Acholi</a> spirit medium who claimed guidance from a spirit called Lakwena. Recruiting mainly Acholi soldiers of the defeated former army, it fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoweri-museveni">Yoweri Museveni</a>'s government in 1986–1987, its followers anointed with oil said to protect them from bullets, and marched south until it was crushed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jinja">Jinja</a> in late 1987.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/holy-spirit-movement.jpg" alt="Holy Spirit Movement" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:BorysMapping · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HSMF_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
